-- ============================================================================
-- InstaCar — full database bootstrap (paste into the Supabase SQL Editor)
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Generated by scripts/build-sql-bundle.mjs. Do not edit by hand.
--
-- What this creates
--   * every table / enum / index of the legacy MySQL dump
--     (users, branches, cars, car_schedules, bookings, booking_payments,
--      booking_photos, booking_remarks, reviews, contact_messages, expenses,
--      site_content, operator_remittances, operator_remittance_photos,
--      staff_fee_remittances, staff_fee_remittance_photos)
--   * the RLS policies and helper functions used by the PHP session logic
--   * the 5 storage buckets + their policies
--       car-images (public)            <- images/cars/*
--       booking-uploads (private)      <- images/ids/<folder>/*
--       booking-photos (private)       <- images/customers/*
--       remittance-photos (private)    <- images/remittances/*
--       site-assets (public)           <- images/qr_code_payment.png
--   * the seed rows from the legacy dump (57 rows, legacy primary keys)
--   * the public.users <-> auth.users link:
--       - BEFORE trigger creates the Supabase Auth shadow row
--       - AFTER triggers keep both tables in sync (password, e-mail, profile)
--       - a self-service sign-up is provisioned into public.users
--       - backfill-auth.sql creates the Auth account of every seeded user
--
-- Every seeded account can sign in with its original password because GoTrue
-- verifies the legacy PHP bcrypt hashes natively.
--
-- It is idempotent: running it twice is harmless.
--
-- After this, upload the images with:
--   node scripts/upload-images.mjs            (cars only)
--   node scripts/upload-images.mjs --scope=all
-- ============================================================================


